/fuzz/corpus/** binary

# Generated output. These paths are re-captured from the binary, not authored,
# so any issue ids inside them are quoted product data, not this commit's work.
#
# The insta goldens are the sharp case: the Issue schema embeds its own doc
# example for the id field on the same single physical line a vocabulary
# change rewrites, so re-capturing one puts that example on an added diff
# line and the attribution guard reads documentation prose as an agent
# marker. The id belongs to the ledger that documented it, not to whichever
# commit happened to re-emit the bytes.
#
# Do not name the example id in these comments. This file is itself staged
# on the commit that adds it, so a literal here is an added line carrying the
# token and the guard blocks the very declaration meant to stop that.
#
# Patterns carry no leading slash: toron's matcher compares them against
# repo-relative paths, and git's own anchoring is not what it does.
#
# This exempts a path from the bead-hunk ATTRIBUTION scan only. A projected
# path still needs a lease: the question here is whose work the id describes,
# not who may write the file.
tests/snapshots/snapshots/** linguist-generated=true
tests/snapshots/agent_baseline/** linguist-generated=true
